THE ANALYSIS ENGINE
===================

Structural analysis does not run in Java. It runs in native code that this mod carries
inside its jar, and there are two shapes of that, one replacing the other:

  * The ENGINE LIBRARY (`libbsi_tectonic.so`, `bsi_tectonic.dll`) — the current shape.
    A shared library the game LOADS. It is not a program, is not started as a process, and
    is unpacked without an execute bit. The mod calls five C functions across a frozen
    interface (`contract/bsi_capi.h`), bound with JNA; there is no custom JNI code. Which
    engine a given jar carries, its version and the interface revision it speaks are all
    recorded in `blockreality-engine/natives.manifest`, filled in by asking the library
    itself rather than by asserting it.

  * The SIDECAR EXECUTABLE (`br-sidecar`, `br-sidecar.exe`) — the earlier shape, being
    retired. A separate program unpacked from the jar and started as a child process.

Nothing is downloaded, at build time or at run time. Both shapes are bytes already inside
the jar the player chose to install, with their SHA-256 recorded beside them, and the
runtime refuses anything whose hash does not match.


THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE
====================

The components below are statically linked into one or other of those binaries, so their
terms travel with every copy of it. Full texts are in `third_party/` in the repository and
in `META-INF/third_party/` inside the jar.

In the ENGINE LIBRARY
---------------------
tectonic2 — Apache License 2.0
    The structural analysis engine. <https://github.com/rocky59487/tectonic2>
    `third_party/tectonic2-Apache2.txt`

OpenBLAS — BSD 3-Clause
    Dense linear algebra kernels. <https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS>
    `third_party/OpenBLAS-BSD3.txt`

LAPACK and LAPACKE — BSD 3-Clause (LAPACKE: Intel variant)
    Factorisation routines, reached through the LAPACKE C interface.
    <http://www.netlib.org/lapack/> — `third_party/LAPACK-BSD3.txt`

METIS — Apache License 2.0
    Fill-reducing ordering for the sparse factorisation.
    <https://github.com/KarypisLab/METIS> — `third_party/METIS-Apache2.txt`

GCC runtime libraries — GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1
    libstdc++, libgcc and libgfortran, linked statically so the shipped library depends on
    nothing but the C runtime. Permitted by the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1.
    `third_party/GCC-Runtime-Library-Exception.txt`

In the SIDECAR EXECUTABLE
-------------------------
FrameCore — MIT License
    The finite element solver. Consumed as an external source dependency that this
    repository does not carry; the three patches this project applies to it are in
    `sidecar/patches/`. `third_party/FrameCore-MIT.txt`

Eigen — Mozilla Public License 2.0
    Linear algebra, used by FrameCore. `br-sidecar` is built with `EIGEN_MPL2_ONLY`, so
    only MPL-2.0 parts of Eigen are compiled in — no LGPL-licensed components.
    `third_party/Eigen-MPL2.txt`

    MPL-2.0 section 3.2 requires that recipients of the binary be told how to obtain the
    source of the covered code. Eigen's source is at <https://gitlab.com/libeigen/eigen>,
    and the exact version a build uses is whatever the building machine's `libeigen3-dev`
    provides — recorded, with the host and every source hash, in
    `evidence/verification.json`. `br-sidecar` itself is built from `sidecar/` in this
    repository and its build is byte-reproducible on a matching toolchain.

NOT STATICALLY LINKED, AND NOT REDISTRIBUTED
--------------------------------------------
JNA (Java Native Access) — Apache License 2.0 or LGPL 2.1, at the recipient's option.
    Used to call the engine library's five C functions. Minecraft already ships JNA, so
    this mod declares it as a compile-time dependency and does NOT carry a copy.


